What this does:

- Removes the call to `str_()` (which today only returns the untranslated template ID in a CLI‐only error path).
- Pulls in the raw UIStrings template (`errorDefinition.message`), does a very shallow “{foo}→value” replacement (enough to handle `{errorCode}` or any other single‐variable templates).
- Leaves you with real English text on CLI fatal errors (e.g. “The URL you have provided appears to be invalid.”).
